t there will be no new groups from the 2e corebook rather than no new groups in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26974-dreamwave","name":"Dreamwave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T15:47:34-07:00","id":1514888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1514852#post1514852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they said that they are not going to disclose the ratio between new and old groups, so we don't know how many of those are actually new besides that among the new Compacts we have the Recalibraters (anti Network Zero) and the Las Guandas (who have a &quot;family list&quot; of enemies) and that among the new conspiracies we have Operation Nebula (Ancient Astronaut Theorists) and the &quot;Watchers&quot; (not their full name, potentially even just a nickname, draw information and skills from their reincarnations)</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as the Watcher don't go the route of &quot;Observe, record, don't interfere&quot; as so many like materials do, then I am soundly interested in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T16:32:32-07:00","id":1514894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1514888#post1514888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So long as the Watcher don't go the route of &quot;Observe, record, don't interfere&quot; as so many like materials do, then I am soundly interested in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell that would be too much like some weird network 0 conspiracy. Sorry for the pointless add-on<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh well. Hopefully Friday","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-15-2023, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T08:13:22-07:00","id":1515246,"title":"","content":"Its out! Keepers of the Source and Night Watch are back!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T09:04:04-07:00","id":1515254,"title":"","content":"I found the Keepers an odd choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T09:10:53-07:00","id":1515256,"title":"","content":"I love how Conspiracies are usually based off actual conspiracies regarding organizations, but Operation Nebula turns it on its head by being a conspiracy made up OF conspiracy theorists who believe a popular conspiracy theory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T09:48:45-07:00","id":1515261,"title":"","content":"Party party party party!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T10:09:45-07:00","id":1515262,"title":"","content":"First Impression score for each of the orgs in Tending the Fire:<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey- 7 (Art gets 9, Logo 9, however, but I feel the writeup doesn't give anything new compared to 1e. AA are still awesome anyway so I can't score it too low)<br /> <br /> Crimson Halo- 9 (Art 8, Logo 10, blown out of the park imho)<br /> <br /> Crossroads Convoy- 7 (Art 7, Logo 8, like they fill a good niche and could maker good stories, but don't fully click as a PC I want to play. Useful as NPCs however)<br /> <br /> Eden Covenant- 6 (Art 5, Logo 7, a bit all over the place and definitely more of antagonists than protagonists).<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source- 8 (Art 8, Logo 8, again don't give much beyond 1e but they do polish a few rough edges imo)<br /> <br /> Las Guadanas- 10 (Art 9, Logo 8, honestly amazing. I didn't thought I would like them from the snip but boy I was wrong! Also, remind me a lot of my Ebony Fangs and I can really see how I can make them into a chapter of the later, which makes them even more of use to me)<br /> <br /> Night Watch- 6 (Art 5, Logo 5, I honestly never clicked with the original 1e writeup and I am not sure they add much more. The fact that the original writeup very much emphasized them being Afro-American and the art misses that part also penalize the score)<br /> <br /> Recalibrators- 7 (Art 7, Logo 5, they are not bad and they fill a good niche, and also not what I was expecting, but again something more that I would use as NPC than as a PC)<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru- 9 (Art 5, Logo 8, Relics 8 which is, honestly, disappointing, but the writeup compensates for it by a lot. They clearly draw upon the extra lore from C&amp;C, and add new twists which wraps it ionto a very cool package. Relics are still cool as they always were)<br /> <br /> Asclepeion- 8 (Art 9, Logo 7, Endowments 9, they are cool and fill the &quot;street doctor&quot; niche that was needed, but something between them being strangely young, a yet another explicitly Greek conspiracy right after the AKD and actually have the AKD in their writeups kinda takes away some of their points. Their Endowments are rad, however, even though I would have prefered them to not be so balantly supernatural)<br /> <br /> Campion Wildlife Service- 7 (Art 7, Logo 7, Endowments 7, the concept is cool, but something feels a bit lacking. Them marking the Deviant conspiracies as enemies is a cool bit, but feels like they would have worked much better as a compact than as a conspiracy. Also, having the founder's name in the title only reinforces this feeling unfortunately. The Endowments also feel a bit.. weird? somewhere between Advanced Armory and Thaumatech. Just too generic imo). <br /> <br /> Enigmatics- 7 (Art 8, Logo 5, Endowments 7 again a cool concept but they are feeling that they are still at that level- a concept. Feels like they need a lot more development. The name is also too shallow imo, another symptom I think. Also, a question mark for a logo? for a group of artists? The Endowments are cool, but too... insidious? They all sound pretty dark. I mean, rewarding cannibalism? Causing insanity? Amnesia? I can see those guys more as slashers than as hunters, honestly)<br /> <br /> Operation Nebula- 8 (Art 9, Logo 9, Endowments 9, my main issue with those guys is that it is not very clear how did they became a conspiracy. Being a group of ancient astronaut theorists and conspiracy theories doesn't really make a material for a conspiracy, and sounds more fitting for a compact. The use of the internet alone is not enough imo. The Endowment itself is pretty cool, with the emphasis on harvesting &quot;alien cores&quot; and all of that)<br /> <br /> Survivor's Club- 6 (Art 10, Logo 10, Endowments 9, feels a lot like a compact, and if they really wanted to present them as a conspiracy they should have just &quot;promoted the Sisterhood imo. Again, not really sure what made them into a conspiracy- a running theme here for most writeups. Still, a way to play Buffy I guess? The Endowments are pretty rad, however)<br /> <br /> Watchers- 8 (Art 8 with an extra bonus for presenting a person with dwarfism, Logo 8, Endowments 8 like I personally made a conspiracy with a very similar concept, but this one suffers a lot from being, again, very shallow in terms of development. The name is, again, too generic. I liked the nod to the Dog Star, but it feels too focused around the Deathless and I would have loved to get a bit more about how they operate when Sothis does not mess shit up, especially as mummies are somewhat more active in 2e. At the very least they are useful as material for my own Avicii Sutra. Endowments are cool though)<br /> <br /> White Hare Society- 9 (Art 10, Logo 8, Endowments 8... Look I can live with the similarities between the Survivors Guide and Aspel's Final Girl Club and the Watchers using the same concept as the Avicii Sutra as it is pretty generic, but the Society being &quot;Portuguese Age of Discovery Conspiracy that roams to Otherworlds sounds <i>a little too similar</i> to the Navio del Tolos... it seems that I am going to need to revise them as I planned to make them a STV release, and I am not going to let my sister's art go to waste. Thankfully the idea of a explorer conspiracy is wide enough to be adapted. Still, can't say anything bad about this writeup considering that I made a very similar conspiracy myself. Anyway, the Endowments are cool, but a bit weird? The use of potions as a medium feels strange imo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T11:02:55-07:00","id":1515266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515262#post1515262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Impression score for each of the orgs in Tending the Fire:<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey- 7 (Art gets 9, Logo 9, however, but I feel the writeup doesn't give anything new compared to 1e. AA are still awesome anyway so I can't score it too low)<br /> <br /> Crimson Halo- 9 (Art 8, Logo 10, blown out of the park imho)<br /> <br /> Crossroads Convoy- 7 (Art 7, Logo 8, like they fill a good niche and could maker good stories, but don't fully click as a PC I want to play. Useful as NPCs however)<br /> <br /> Eden Covenant- 6 (Art 5, Logo 7, a bit all over the place and definitely more of antagonists than protagonists).<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source- 8 (Art 8, Logo 8, again don't give much beyond 1e but they do polish a few rough edges imo)<br /> <br /> Las Guadanas- 10 (Art 9, Logo 8, honestly amazing. I didn't thought I would like them from the snip but boy I was wrong! Also, remind me a lot of my Ebony Fangs and I can really see how I can make them into a chapter of the later, which makes them even more of use to me)<br /> <br /> Night Watch- 6 (Art 5, Logo 5, I honestly never clicked with the original 1e writeup and I am not sure they add much more. The fact that the original writeup very much emphasized them being Afro-American and the art misses that part also penalize the score)<br /> <br /> Recalibrators- 7 (Art 7, Logo 5, they are not bad and they fill a good niche, and also not what I was expecting, but again something more that I would use as NPC than as a PC)<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru- 9 (Art 5, Logo 8, Relics 8 which is, honestly, disappointing, but the writeup compensates for it by a lot. They clearly draw upon the extra lore from C&amp;C, and add new twists which wraps it ionto a very cool package. Relics are still cool as they always were)<br /> <br /> Asclepeion- 8 (Art 9, Logo 7, Endowments 9, they are cool and fill the &quot;street doctor&quot; niche that was needed, but something between them being strangely young, a yet another explicitly Greek conspiracy right after the AKD and actually have the AKD in their writeups kinda takes away some of their points. Their Endowments are rad, however, even though I would have prefered them to not be so balantly supernatural)<br /> <br /> Campion Wildlife Service- 7 (Art 7, Logo 7, Endowments 7, the concept is cool, but something feels a bit lacking. Them marking the Deviant conspiracies as enemies is a cool bit, but feels like they would have worked much better as a compact than as a conspiracy. Also, having the founder's name in the title only reinforces this feeling unfortunately. The Endowments also feel a bit.. weird? somewhere between Advanced Armory and Thaumatech. Just too generic imo).<br /> <br /> Enigmatics- 7 (Art 8, Logo 5, Endowments 7 again a cool concept but they are feeling that they are still at that level- a concept. Feels like they need a lot more development. The name is also too shallow imo, another symptom I think. Also, a question mark for a logo? for a group of artists? The Endowments are cool, but too... insidious? They all sound pretty dark. I mean, rewarding cannibalism? Causing insanity? Amnesia? I can see those guys more as slashers than as hunters, honestly)<br /> <br /> Operation Nebula- 8 (Art 9, Logo 9, Endowments 9, my main issue with those guys is that it is not very clear how did they became a conspiracy. Being a group of ancient astronaut theorists and conspiracy theories doesn't really make a material for a conspiracy, and sounds more fitting for a compact. The use of the internet alone is not enough imo. The Endowment itself is pretty cool, with the emphasis on harvesting &quot;alien cores&quot; and all of that)<br /> <br /> Survivor's Club- 6 (Art 10, Logo 10, Endowments 9, feels a lot like a compact, and if they really wanted to present them as a conspiracy they should have just &quot;promoted the Sisterhood imo. Again, not really sure what made them into a conspiracy- a running theme here for most writeups. Still, a way to play Buffy I guess? The Endowments are pretty rad, however)<br /> <br /> Watchers- 8 (Art 8 with an extra bonus for presenting a person with dwarfism, Logo 8, Endowments 8 like I personally made a conspiracy with a very similar concept, but this one suffers a lot from being, again, very shallow in terms of development. The name is, again, too generic. I liked the nod to the Dog Star, but it feels too focused around the Deathless and I would have loved to get a bit more about how they operate when Sothis does not mess shit up, especially as mummies are somewhat more active in 2e. At the very least they are useful as material for my own Avicii Sutra. Endowments are cool though)<br /> <br /> White Hare Society- 9 (Art 10, Logo 8, Endowments 8... Look I can live with the similarities between the Survivors Guide and Aspel's Final Girl Club and the Watchers using the same concept as the Avicii Sutra as it is pretty generic, but the Society being &quot;Portuguese Age of Discovery Conspiracy that roams to Otherworlds sounds <i>a little too similar</i> to the Navio del Tolos... it seems that I am going to need to revise them as I planned to make them a STV release, and I am not going to let my sister's art go to waste. Thankfully the idea of a explorer conspiracy is wide enough to be adapted. Still, can't say anything bad about this writeup considering that I made a very similar conspiracy myself. Anyway, the Endowments are cool, but a bit weird? The use of potions as a medium feels strange imo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Word count has definitely been a blow to the new compacts and conspiracies. But oh well, it just gives me more room to create my own flourishes for my games. I would like more though on all of them<br /> <br /> EDIT: I will say I do disagree about Enigmatics seeming more like slashers. While the endowment is certainly insidious, they are a movement based on witnessing the supernatural and gaining mad inspiration from it. I think seeing them as slashers is doing them a dishonor. They are a great example of a Conspiracy that's playing with forces they truly don't understand. It's a great way to show that Conspiracies can cause harm to regular humans simply as a by product of harnessing supernatural forces. Seeing them as slashers instead shifts that from a tragic case of a broken group of people projecting their traumas outwards in an unhealthy way, to being a more generic &quot;mad artist&quot;. And again, they ARE primarily focused on supernatural encounters. I do agree that they need more though. The word count hits hard","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-16-2023, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T00:50:59-07:00","id":1515333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515266#post1515266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: I will say I do disagree about Enigmatics seeming more like slashers. While the endowment is certainly insidious, they are a movement based on witnessing the supernatural and gaining mad inspiration from it. I think seeing them as slashers is doing them a dishonor. They are a great example of a Conspiracy that's playing with forces they truly don't understand. It's a great way to show that Conspiracies can cause harm to regular humans simply as a by product of harnessing supernatural forces. Seeing them as slashers instead shifts that from a tragic case of a broken group of people projecting their traumas outwards in an unhealthy way, to being a more generic &quot;mad artist&quot;. And again, they ARE primarily focused on supernatural encounters. I do agree that they need more though. The word count hits hard</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with the Enigmatics is very simple- their Vigil is explicitly non-violent. Now, don't get me wrong, I am totally fine with such groups, and they occupy a important niche of inspired artists which is really cool. However, their Endowments are <i>really dangerous</i>, especially for regular humans. You can call it &quot;playing with fire&quot;, but again- those hunters do not focus on killing monsters, only by being inspired by them, and a lot of the harms are very much directed towards regular people (for example, turning people into cannibals, or having statues that demand human sacrifice, This.. ain't good. A non violent group which makes some very dangerous Endowments they don't fully control that are not meant to be applicable in the Vigil and has some very, very bad consequences for mortals is a very bad combinations for everyone around. I am not saying &quot;those guys are slashers&quot;, but saying &quot;are you sure they are not?&quot; because either intentionally or not, it is not clear to me how their Endowments actually help their own Vigil of getting inspired by monsters or the Vigil as a whole. Even if they are not outright slashers- well, they are foot and a half in the way, imo. This is basically turns to, again, &quot;how is this a conspiracy when all of their powers are environmental hazard&quot; . Good concept, sure, but God it needs much more development to become playable imo.<br /> <br /> EDIT- note that if they were a violent group it would have made at least some sense for how they are using their Endowments for the Vigil. Again, I personally like the idea of artists being non violent in terms of their Vigil, but in that case the Endowments can't be so violent- because someone is meant to get hurt, and ion most instances the texts explicitly says that bystanders are going to be the ones getting screwed. It can't be a matter of wordcount alone considering that other orgs do not generally suffer from this dissonance (some have their own problems, as I mentioned before)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-17-2023, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T05:12:48-07:00","id":1515349,"title":"","content":"Ok, I finished reading the supplement, overall I give it a positive grade because it's full of exciting ideas to create games focused on organizations and social intrigue.<br /> That said, on the negative, I will say one word that came to my mind constantly while reading: rushed. There are just not enough words dedicated to some of the compacts and conspiracies to flesh them out and as a result, sometimes I get confused about what exactly is the role of the organization and what I'm supposed to do with them. I get there are space constrictions, but given the number of pages, I think it wouldn't have been unreasonable to add one or two pages more to each compact and conspiracy.<br /> Then there's what some have mentioned before, some conspiracies feel more like compacts and vice-versa, and also some read as if the only reason they really exist is to support other hunter organizations or that their objective is unrelated to the vigil and only hunt monsters as a side activity, great as npc characters and factions, but not so much as player characters. Again, another page or two would have gone a long way in helping to know them better and clarifying how to better use them.<br /> I want to end on a positive note and emphasize that I liked the supplement, there's plenty to use. I just wish it could have been longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-18-2023, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T05:25:53-07:00","id":1515350,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, I can't see a quick reference to which Conspiracy relates to which Endowments. It's not hard, they did spell out in the Endowments section but...I'd find it helpful.<br /> <br /> So here it is:<ul><li>Aegis Kai Doru - Relics (as before)</li> <li>Asclepeion - Enkoimesis (mystical healing)</li> <li>Campion Wildlife Service - Animal Control Kit (tools of the trade &amp; extracted mutations)</li> <li>Enigmatics - Inspiration (magical masterwork art pieces)</li> <li>Operation Nebula - Xenotechnology (Gizmos made from salvaged &quot;alien&quot; technology)</li> <li>Survivor's Club - The Horror Within (embracing the &quot;scourge&quot; ie the slasher &quot;virus&quot; within)</li> <li>Watchers - Lives Remembered (knowledge leveraged from past &amp; future lives)</li> <li>White Hare Society - Infusion (alchemically infused earthly components with otherworldly energies)</li> </ul>Given the limited write ups, I do feel the Endowments help with the feel of the new Conspiracies.<br /> As an example, The Survivor's Club comes off a lot darker and more dangerous when you know it isn't just a bunch of survivors playing Buffy, and they are doing the whole &quot;using the power of their own archnemesis&quot; things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:10:54-07:00","id":1515361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515333#post1515333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with the Enigmatics is very simple- their Vigil is explicitly non-violent. Now, don't get me wrong, I am totally fine with such groups, and they occupy a important niche of inspired artists which is really cool. However, their Endowments are <i>really dangerous</i>, especially for regular humans. You can call it &quot;playing with fire&quot;, but again- those hunters do not focus on killing monsters, only by being inspired by them, and a lot of the harms are very much directed towards regular people (for example, turning people into cannibals, or having statues that demand human sacrifice, This.. ain't good. A non violent group which makes some very dangerous Endowments they don't fully control that are not meant to be applicable in the Vigil and has some very, very bad consequences for mortals is a very bad combinations for everyone around. I am not saying &quot;those guys are slashers&quot;, but saying &quot;are you sure they are not?&quot; because either intentionally or not, it is not clear to me how their Endowments actually help their own Vigil of getting inspired by monsters or the Vigil as a whole. Even if they are not outright slashers- well, they are foot and a half in the way, imo. This is basically turns to, again, &quot;how is this a conspiracy when all of their powers are environmental hazard&quot; . Good concept, sure, but God it needs much more development to become playable imo.<br /> <br /> EDIT- note that if they were a violent group it would have made at least some sense for how they are using their Endowments for the Vigil. Again, I personally like the idea of artists being non violent in terms of their Vigil, but in that case the Endowments can't be so violent- because someone is meant to get hurt, and ion most instances the texts explicitly says that bystanders are going to be the ones getting screwed. It can't be a matter of wordcount alone considering that other orgs do not generally suffer from this dissonance (some have their own problems, as I mentioned before)</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good points. I actually agree. I had a knee jerk reaction to the slashers comment (which is a warranted concern you have. It's no issue of word count that they harm regular people so much)<br /> <br /> i think what they need for the Vigil is a direction to be taken in regards to their influence. The Enigmatics are a movement, one that is supernatural in nature considering they lose Inspiration when they no longer associate with it. Personally, I'm thinking if Network 0 wants to prove the supernatural exist, and Null Mysteriis wants to understand the supernatural, then the Enigmatics want to inspire (of course) attitudes toward the supernatural. <br /> <br /> Taking this into account, I would make the Enigmatics the cultural influences of the Vigil. While their Endowments would still be dangerous to the minds of those who witness it, the artworks would primarily twist the hearts and minds of its viewers in a way that may lead to worship, contempt, or twisted emulation and insight into the supernatural. Of course, the artworks would still have minds of their own. However, I'd make sure that they really represent the Enigmatic's interpretation of the supernatural, and in this way the artwork imitates what it's based on while also negatively affecting monsters.<br /> <br /> It's a work in progress, obviously. But i do think you're right about the Enigmatics needing more than just concept. <br /> <br /> I'm more focused on Operation Nebula though. I actually love the twist, but they do need more to their ideals. I actually love that they work through a fragmented dark net thing, as it reinforces the idea the Operators dont actually trust each other beyond the ASSUMPTION their efforts to piece together events and such means they MAY be actual humans, but you're right that they need something more. As of now, anyone could gain Operator Endowments and know all about the conspiracy with enough internet know how. I'm thinking about making them part of an exile emerging into its own God machine, with operation Nebula as Infrastructure, but I'm not sold on the idea completely. I just think their paranoia and lethal joke conspiracy status should be maintained","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:11:28-07:00","id":1515362,"title":"","content":"It says my post in unapproved. Did I do something wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T08:15:32-07:00","id":1515375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515362#post1515362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says my post in unapproved. Did I do something wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a bug in the forums where if you edit your post too quickly after posting or between editions it is marked as spam","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T09:43:41-07:00","id":1515382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515375#post1515375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a bug in the forums where if you edit your post too quickly after posting or between editions it is marked as spam</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well it happened as soon as I posted. Can yall see it? It was a response to you regarding the Enigmatics (it's mostly me agreeing on your points before going on a tangent with Nebula. I did leave out I completely agree on the logo not making sense)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:00:08-07:00","id":1515389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515382#post1515382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, well it happened as soon as I posted. Can yall see it? It was a response to you regarding the Enigmatics (it's mostly me agreeing on your points before going on a tangent with Nebula. I did leave out I completely agree on the logo not making sense)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately we can't see it. Either wait a day or two for a moderator or delete and post again I think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:09:10-07:00","id":1515395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515333#post1515333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with the Enigmatics is very simple- their Vigil is explicitly non-violent. Now, don't get me wrong, I am totally fine with such groups, and they occupy a important niche of inspired artists which is really cool. However, their Endowments are <i>really dangerous</i>, especially for regular humans. You can call it &quot;playing with fire&quot;, but again- those hunters do not focus on killing monsters, only by being inspired by them, and a lot of the harms are very much directed towards regular people (for example, turning people into cannibals, or having statues that demand human sacrifice, This.. ain't good. A non violent group which makes some very dangerous Endowments they don't fully control that are not meant to be applicable in the Vigil and has some very, very bad consequences for mortals is a very bad combinations for everyone around. I am not saying &quot;those guys are slashers&quot;, but saying &quot;are you sure they are not?&quot; because either intentionally or not, it is not clear to me how their Endowments actually help their own Vigil of getting inspired by monsters or the Vigil as a whole. Even if they are not outright slashers- well, they are foot and a half in the way, imo. This is basically turns to, again, &quot;how is this a conspiracy when all of their powers are environmental hazard&quot; . Good concept, sure, but God it needs much more development to become playable imo.<br /> <br /> EDIT- note that if they were a violent group it would have made at least some sense for how they are using their Endowments for the Vigil. Again, I personally like the idea of artists being non violent in terms of their Vigil, but in that case the Endowments can't be so violent- because someone is meant to get hurt, and ion most instances the texts explicitly says that bystanders are going to be the ones getting screwed. It can't be a matter of wordcount alone considering that other orgs do not generally suffer from this dissonance (some have their own problems, as I mentioned before)</div> </div> </div> </div>Second try<br /> <br /> Very good points. I actually agree. I had a knee jerk reaction to the slashers comment (which is a warranted concern you have. It's no issue of word count that they harm regular people so much)<br /> <br /> i think what they need for the Vigil is a direction to be taken in regards to their influence. The Enigmatics are a movement, one that is supernatural in nature considering they lose Inspiration when they no longer associate with it. Personally, I'm thinking if Network 0 wants to prove the supernatural exist, and Null Mysteriis wants to understand the supernatural, then the Enigmatics want to inspire (of course) attitudes toward the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Taking this into account, I would make the Enigmatics the cultural influences of the Vigil. While their Endowments would still be dangerous to the minds of those who witness it, the artworks would primarily twist the hearts and minds of its viewers in a way that may lead to worship, contempt, or twisted emulation and insight into the supernatural. Of course, the artworks would still have minds of their own. However, I'd make sure that they really represent the Enigmatic's interpretation of the supernatural, and in this way the artwork imitates what it's based on while also negatively affecting monsters.<br /> <br /> It's a work in progress, obviously. But i do think you're right about the Enigmatics needing more than just concept.<br /> <br /> I'm more focused on Operation Nebula though. I actually love the twist, but they do need more to their ideals. I actually love that they work through a fragmented dark net thing, as it reinforces the idea the Operators dont actually trust each other beyond the ASSUMPTION their efforts to piece together events and such means they MAY be actual humans, but you're right that they need something more. As of now, anyone could gain Operator Endowments and know all about the conspiracy with enough internet know how. I'm thinking about making them part of an exile emerging into its own God machine, with operation Nebula as Infrastructure, but I'm not sold on the idea completely. I just think their paranoia and lethal joke conspiracy status should be maintained\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:23:31-07:00","id":1515400,"title":"","content":"I guess I'll have to wait. Maybe it's a spoiler thing I'm violating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T14:57:36-07:00","id":1515420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515333#post1515333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the Enigmatics is very simple- their Vigil is explicitly non-violent. Now, don't get me wrong, I am totally fine with such groups, and they occupy a important niche of inspired artists which is really cool. However, their Endowments are <i>really dangerous</i>, especially for regular humans. You can call it &quot;playing with fire&quot;, but again- those hunters do not focus on killing monsters, only by being inspired by them, and a lot of the harms are very much directed towards regular people (for example, turning people into cannibals, or having statues that demand human sacrifice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunger of the Wolf makes normal people who hear it crave flesh in a way that's mechanically represented by taking the Spooked Condition if they resist the urge, and its primary Vigil-relevant effect is that it makes monsters using Dread Powers run out of Willpower faster. The Red Wax Mask animates statues until dawn and can be paid for with the user's blood to the same degree as its normal activation cost (and I here note that the vampire blood used to make the Mask didn't come from nowhere). The conspiracy doesn't <i>focus on</i> killing monsters, but that doesn't mean they don't do so at all<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not saying &quot;those guys are slashers&quot;, but saying &quot;are you sure they are not?&quot; because either intentionally or not, it is not clear to me how their Endowments actually help their own Vigil of getting inspired by monsters or the Vigil as a whole. Even if they are not outright slashers- well, they are foot and a half in the way, imo. </div> </div> </div>Lost, I'll be frank, this smacks of using a term with a specific meaning as a general &quot;it's bad&quot; word \u2014 a slasher is a human driven to murder people. I should not have to tell you that this is more than a full step in the opposite direction from &quot;monster-hunters who don't focus on killing monsters.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I personally like the idea of artists being non violent in terms of their Vigil, but in that case the Endowments can't be so violent- because someone is meant to get hurt, and ion most instances the texts explicitly says that bystanders are going to be the ones getting screwed. </div> </div> </div>The very extremely obvious workaround for this, which the creator of a masterwork will know because any successful roll to create a masterwork tells you how the thing works \u2014 is to not use the thing around bystanders in uncontrolled circumstances. The Recalibrators demonstrate that enough hunters understand this concept to build a compact around it.<br /> <br /> Masterworks created through Inspiration are supernaturally-empowered artworks with their own malevolent agenda. Our presented examples run as follows:<br /> 1. A painting inspired by struggles against demonic temptation, which can make observers looking upon it for (typically multiple) minutes at a time recover a Willpower and become Addicting to it, allowing them to gain more Willpower from fulfilling their Vice within view of it at the cost of all other sources of Willpower recovery; addicted monsters also become Obsessed with having and showing the painting and gain a Vice for the purposes of the painting's effects; the Enigmatic can render addicted characters in the painting's immediate presence Insensate and then Traumatized/Insane, Tiltwise, ending the Addiction and Obsession for anyone outside the painting's immediate presence. Relatively harmless for a Depraved Art storyhook and you can use it as a lure for monsters if you're playing the long game in a social context.<br /> 2. A song inspired by an encounter with a werewolf eating a family, which makes monsters' Dread Powers more costly to use and tempts humans to eat human flesh for Willpower and a first-time breaking point or be Spooked enough to resist; the song lives in one head at a time and wants to have its power used, so its host may find themselves singing it unconsciously unless they catch themselves, a Dramatic Failure on the activation roll lets it jump to someone else's head for the chapter, and anyone who's engaged in cannibalism retains a full copy of the masterwork afterward and can spread it to others. Solid way to deprive a monster of their cost-bearing abilities, good rationale to strengthen your Resolve and get better at Inspiration and not use it to confront monsters around people you think might be proactive about consuming human flesh if given the opportunity.<br /> 3. Scrimshaw disks depicting aquatic monsters, which dramatically enhance rolls to go unnoticed except to a specific category of people that varies by specific masterwork, with whom the Enigmatic becomes mutually Swooned; the cost is becoming Deprived until the user fulfills their Vice or spends a scene with their Touchstone, and until then they'll sleepwalk toward a body of water or the nearest other such masterwork. Mild touch of the Depraved Artist, mild touch of occult romance, not exactly popping with deadly intent on its own unless you have some particular ideas about why cursed objects might be trying to get together.<br /> 4. A bust of Pallas Athena inspired by witnessing things mortals shouldn't see, which offers knowledge in exchange for memories of secrets based on the success of the activation roll; regardless of the outcome, the player always has the option of losing the memories temporarily, only a Dramatic Failure results in permanent loss of an important memory, and the character can choose what memories they're sacrificing by making the memory loss more severe. Obviously the product of a traumatic experience and doesn't have any direct effect on bystanders at all because it only affects the user by trading memories for knowledge.<br /> 5. A mask cast from a monster's face using wax mixed with vampire blood. Animates all statues within range below a certain Size to act as basic Retainers for the rest of the night, returning to their original poses at dawn; the mask must be fed with the user's blood to activate, and in the last hour before dawn, the statues seek out people (including, potentially, the user) to sacrifice to bathe the mask in their blood, and if the mask does not receive such a tithe by dawn, it inflicts another point of lethal damage on the user. A fairly dire power to use for a fairly difficult masterwork to create, but this one notably doesn't have any side-effects based around compelling its use and, even if you rule that monsters don't count as people for the purposes of the mask's criteria, it's tailor-made for dealing with monsters with a retinue.<br /> <br /> I frankly wouldn't consider these meaningfully more morally iffy for a hunter conspiracy to be using than the full span of effects demonstrated by tokens in 1e Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T11:50:23-07:00","id":1515467,"title":"","content":"So question, when will this come out to the general public? I'm very excited for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4336-crinosg","name":"CrinosG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T14:09:45-07:00","id":1515476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrinosG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515467#post1515467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So question, when will this come out to the general public? I'm very excited for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>After the errata collection phase has finished and the various corrections from that phase have been made. For a book of this size, give it somewhere between a couple weeks and a month, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T17:29:11-07:00","id":1515502,"title":"","content":"To add to the &quot;compromised by monsters&quot; list, we have:<br /> <br /> Probably and Inexplicably Linked to the Fairy Order of Oneirophysics (Asclepion)<br /> Likely An Extended Cult for the Deceived (Enigmatics)<br /> Probably Half-Directed by Either a Changeling or a Demon or a Demon in a Changeling's Cover (Operation Nebula)<br /> A Bunch of Near-Slashers Commiting to Acts Likely To Make Them Full-Slashers (Survivor's Club)<br /> I'm Not Sure What Arisen Bullshit This Is Exactly, But It's Some Kind of Arisen-Adjacent Bullshit, Unless It's Astral Bullshit, Or Both (Watchers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T00:46:06-07:00","id":1515519,"title":"","content":"In the context of Operation Nebula it should be worth to mention the Visitors, as they are basically Ancient Aliens. The leaders of Operation Nebula wear tinfoil hats not because they are afraid of aliens controlling their minds- it is so you won't see the holes in the skulls made by the aliens who do control their minds :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T02:57:26-07:00","id":1515522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515333#post1515333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with the Enigmatics is very simple- their Vigil is explicitly non-violent. Now, don't get me wrong, I am totally fine with such groups, and they occupy a important niche of inspired artists which is really cool. However, their Endowments are <i>really dangerous</i>, especially for regular humans. You can call it &quot;playing with fire&quot;, but again- those hunters do not focus on killing monsters, only by being inspired by them, and a lot of the harms are very much directed towards regular people (for example, turning people into cannibals, or having statues that demand human sacrifice, This.. ain't good. A non violent group which makes some very dangerous Endowments they don't fully control that are not meant to be applicable in the Vigil and has some very, very bad consequences for mortals is a very bad combinations for everyone around. I am not saying &quot;those guys are slashers&quot;, but saying &quot;are you sure they are not?&quot; because either intentionally or not, it is not clear to me how their Endowments actually help their own Vigil of getting inspired by monsters or the Vigil as a whole. Even if they are not outright slashers- well, they are foot and a half in the way, imo. This is basically turns to, again, &quot;how is this a conspiracy when all of their powers are environmental hazard&quot; . Good concept, sure, but God it needs much more development to become playable imo.<br /> <br /> EDIT- note that if they were a violent group it would have made at least some sense for how they are using their Endowments for the Vigil. Again, I personally like the idea of artists being non violent in terms of their Vigil, but in that case the Endowments can't be so violent- because someone is meant to get hurt, and ion most instances the texts explicitly says that bystanders are going to be the ones getting screwed. It can't be a matter of wordcount alone considering that other orgs do not generally suffer from this dissonance (some have their own problems, as I mentioned before)</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Vigil doesn\u2019t need to be violent, because they\u2019re focused on the inspiration from the encounter. There\u2019s no oath of pacifism, though. How violent a given Enigmatic might be is their own call. The artist hiding in the bushes with a sketchbook while other hunters deal with the threat is certainly valid, but so is the one that donates a cursed painting to gather a monster nest in one place before lighting the whole place on fire. They\u2019re still hunters, and they can still have a moral compass that drives them to do something about particularly problematic monsters. They also (probably) can\u2019t create their art if they\u2019re dead, so unless the only monsters they encounter are things like Batman With Fangs, they\u2019re likely going to need to defend themselves sooner or later.<br /> Their masterworks are all cursed, yes, and many do have negative effects on innocent bystanders. This requires them to take a creative approach to using them if they wish to minimize collateral damage. An Enigmatic who\u2019s too cavalier about activating their masterworks is walking a slippery slope, and can easily draw the ire of other hunters or even become a particularly twisted slasher. A song that makes Dread Powers harder to use can be handy, but it\u2019s better to use in an isolated area than on a crowded subway car if it also gives mortal bystanders a taste for long pork.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T09:30:25-07:00","id":1515542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515522#post1515522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their Vigil doesn\u2019t need to be violent, because they\u2019re focused on the inspiration from the encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to move a third of a house, so I don't have time to go into it right now, but I pretty firmly disagree with both you and LostLight-the Vigil is inherently a commitment to harm against communities of non-humans for a wide variety of reasons. That said, that violence need not always be physical, and I think there's something messed up about the invasive and expository nature of the Enigmatics masterworks to the supernatural members who are basically being outed under the guise of art, and that's long before accounting for the willful creation of malevolent entities with various abilities to act on communities, or the fact that these masterworks are metaphysically empowered likely means that it could also be used to discern more about the mystic nature of the monsters to those able to check for associated bans, banes, and other such things. It's as easily violent as anything done by Network Zero or Aegis Kai Doru<br /> <br /> But then again, I think a very big part of Vigil is getting people to question what they mean by violence, harm, and the moral and ethical concerns that come from needing to rely on those forms in an overall scenario where the power structures are leant heavily against the powerless, so small wonder I saw it this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-19-2023, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T13:05:09-07:00","id":1515553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515542#post1515542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But then again, I think a very big part of Vigil is getting people to question what they mean by violence, harm, and the moral and ethical concerns that come from needing to rely on those forms in an overall scenario where the power structures are leant heavily against the powerless, so small wonder I saw it this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangent on that- it kinds of remind me a Philosophy Tube video where they talked about what is &quot;violence&quot;, and they gave an interpretation of it being any act which reduces the agency of another being, or &quot;reducing a entity to an object&quot;. In that regard, the Vigil is always violent towards monsters, as it is always about directly reducing the agency of monsters- for example, forcing them out of their hiding places even if they are not interested in it just so you will be &quot;inspired&quot; for a new work of art.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T13:36:54-07:00","id":1515557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515553#post1515553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangent on that- it kinds of remind me a Philosophy Tube video where they talked about what is &quot;violence&quot;, and they gave an interpretation of it being any act which reduces the agency of another being, or &quot;reducing a entity to an object&quot;. In that regard, the Vigil is always violent towards monsters, as it is always about directly reducing the agency of monsters- for example, forcing them out of their hiding places even if they are not interested in it just so you will be &quot;inspired&quot; for a new work of art.</div> </div> </div> </div>PBS's Idea Channel had two videos, one on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qvSd_opycoI\" target=\"_blank\">Undertale</a> and one directly on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DyitF-6tBu4&amp;t=642s\" target=\"_blank\">violence</a>, that generally discuss it in similar ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T17:14:43-07:00","id":1515589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515542#post1515542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I need to move a third of a house, so I don't have time to go into it right now, but I pretty firmly disagree with both you and LostLight-the Vigil is inherently a commitment to harm against communities of non-humans for a wide variety of reasons. That said, that violence need not always be physical, and I think there's something messed up about the invasive and expository nature of the Enigmatics masterworks to the supernatural members who are basically being outed under the guise of art, and that's long before accounting for the willful creation of malevolent entities with various abilities to act on communities, or the fact that these masterworks are metaphysically empowered likely means that it could also be used to discern more about the mystic nature of the monsters to those able to check for associated bans, banes, and other such things. It's as easily violent as anything done by Network Zero or Aegis Kai Doru<br /> <br /> But then again, I think a very big part of Vigil is getting people to question what they mean by violence, harm, and the moral and ethical concerns that come from needing to rely on those forms in an overall scenario where the power structures are leant heavily against the powerless, so small wonder I saw it this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make an excellent point. It\u2019s easy to get hung up on the physical aspect of violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T19:28:11-07:00","id":1515816,"title":"","content":"Anyways, it occurs to me I have no laid out opinions, so on that note:<br /> <br /> Compacts, Least to Most Favorite<br /> <br /> 8) The Recalibrators: When I first heard about this compact idea, my initial response was &quot;Wait, isn't it that just low-budget Valkyrie?&quot;, and on this side of the release, I kind of find myself feel myself confirmed. While I definitely appreciate giving credit towards janitorial services in that way that Hunter can and does do and is part of it's point, and I'm always for that &quot;this would be a cult if they weren't hunters&quot; vibe, I find myself not clicking with the compact as a whole-mostly, it feels like the buck stops at it's concept.<br /> <br /> 7) The Crossroads Convoy: It's not the sort of thing that comes up a lot here, but I fucking love road culture. I love road trips, I love driving all variety of cars from high end sports cars to rinky dink cans you're afraid of falling apart at 85 MPH, I have this weird affinity for gas stations that basically makes them the stores I will visit the most in any given location I'm in, so much so that I have mourned the loss of one in my college days, I enjoy hanging out with those in the land transport business when I get the chance to regardless of their political dispositions, and I feel like if trucking were as profitable and supported as it was before the late 70s, I'd be very down for it. Midnight Roads is one of my unsung favorite supplements over here in Chronicles land, and it's very much part of the reason why I have love for the Knights of Saint Adrian, as road culture is frequently a hand-in-hand companion with the life of bounty hunters, and going into Dark Eras, I've got a soft spot for the Gallow's Post. So imagine my surprise when I found myself cold on the compact handling all of that, even arguably going so far as to be a Hunter variant on the Gallow's Post. I'm not even really sure why that's the case, but it feels, again, a bit like the execution doesn't go a whole lot longer than the concept. Still, I'd rather have it than not, so.<br /> <br /> 6) The Keepers of the Source: If you asked me what the second choice for old compacts to revive for this books should've been, I would've argued the Promethean Brotherhood, but that's a distinctly me problem because I hate the bands you like and there's a lot to like about the Keepers. The conflict of pacifism as an ideal against the needs that violence address, all the questions that go around the subject of defending land contrasted with commiting violence against communities doubly complicated by the metaphors of monstrosity, the softcore occultism that gets into questions of the place for concepts validity in terms of spiritual expressions and satisfactions, as well as questions about the cannibalization of legit folk practice into the commercial forms offered with New Age movements-the Keepers have a lot of things going on that make them likable, actionable, and compelling. I could never really personally grok it, though, and I was vaguely hoping there'd be a sharper presentation to actually get me hooked, but, and I say this as praise, the write-up's as good as it was in Witch Hunters. That means you have a really solid compact that still unfortunately doesn't do anything for me, but hey, it can't always be about me.<br /> <br /> 5) The Eden Covenant: I disagree with Lostlight a fair number of times, and this was one of those that made it clear I needed to make my voice heard, because not only do I not think this compact is not all over the place, the only reason it's in the lower half of the compact list is because I have to admit that I can't see myself playing as one, a position that is only shared with the Recalibrators as this list goes. That said, the focus on dopplegangers is a very versatile focus I'm glad to see be played with, and it's juxtaposition with the power and resource brought in by the co-option with a hateful Christian Televangelist not only unifies the themes of othering that the compact is contesting with, but by neccesity forces it to dig into the myriad moral and ethical questions that should be explored with the theme. It's also a very on point of how Hunter explores ideas around the conflict of idealism against power, as the hateful evangelism forms a very real devil's bargain that's understandable and appreciable even as it manages to be reprehensible. Also, there's something brilliant and darkly hilarious that it's ultimate conflict is in conservative, capitalist Christianity's disgust at an entity whose ultimate journey is iconographized through a very significant Christian experience and practice. I know writers who use subtext, and they're all cowards indeed.<br /> <br /> 4) Ashwood Abbey: Welcome back to the party, baby. Yep, it's the compact everyone loves to hate, and speaking as someone who has had a long road that started with loathing them to loving to loathe them, I'm glad to see Hunter stick to it's thematic guns on them. That said, they are the Abbey, and of all of the organizations brought back that really needed to incorporate as much related text from the supplements, it was the Abbey, which makes it disappointing that it's mostly just a cleaned up version of the First Edition Core's take on them, though appreciably being more clear that they do have lines they don't cross about it. On the other hand, the Abbey's power is one of those things that just comes out of the gate, and love them or hate them, would play them or would swear off anyone who would play them, the Abbey continues to do what they've always done been-be in-your-face transgressive, make you confront yourself, have more fun hunting monsters than you are, and look damn good doing it.<br /> <br /> 3) Crimson Halo: Sex work is work, we love to see a prostitute gack a motherfucker. One could effectively make the argument that the Crimson Halo is to the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood what Night Watch is to The Union, and one would be right, and the more you grok everything in that, the more you understand how fucking badass this compact is. Really, I don't have a whole lot to say other than we stan, Yas Queen, Slay.<br /> <br /> 2) Night Watch: Oh hey, look at that, who would've guessed. Night Watch being a choice supplemental compact to be restored is not surprising to me at all, given how strong and good a concept it was in the first books, and how very neccesary it was for engaging with class issues that the corebook was not always good at addressing. The revamp here is also the only one that does a lot to improve on it's overall concept, namely because it's factions are much more practical and utilitarian than the olds ones which were effectively just another form Status, and thus more useful for charatcer creation and single-roganization party composition. I do agree with the grouse about the artwork-while I can see an argument being made that it doesn't want to lean on the association of minorities with crime, given Night Watch's emphasis on marginalized communities needing to come together for mutual defense and getting resources however they can, I think that argument falls flat and the representation would be a great substantive approach-but otherwise, yeah, love to see the street angels back.<br /> <br /> 1) Las Guada\u00f1as: This is probably some kind of very particular stereotype I should probably have more of a problem with, but a) I'm not sure what that stereotype is beyond Robert Rodriguez movies, and b) this shit is my jam, okay? There's just something to the death-cult-criminal badass acting as violent monster hunter and psychopomp that is just really fucking cool, and for as simple of the write up is, it drips cool for me. Having been raised on the US/Mexican border and having very strong opinions about how my peers get treated in today's society, I've also got a bias for Hispanic and Latinx representation, even if the criminal element and focus on Santa Muerta is kind of really boring (arguably bad) association. If I were to leverage a complaint against them, it might that it steps a little too much on the toes of the Jagged Crescent in the Ascending Ones, particularly since psychopompery is also a giant part of their makeup, but that's honestly a nitpick and I'd rather have a blast playing one in any situation that would reasonably call for it. Hasta la muerte, compadres. *<br /> <br /> *Apologies for the mistyping, this computer makes getting the accents annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T14:05:48-07:00","id":1515894,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> you are always welcome to disagree with me. It is much better than me just talking to myself online :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T16:48:36-07:00","id":1515911,"title":"","content":"I will admit I'm sad Division 6 or promethean brotherhood didn't make it. But Night Watch is satisfying enough. I disliked the claims that they should just be the union, so them being included again I hope fully gets rid of that notion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T09:02:10-07:00","id":1515953,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Division 6 would have been in a very awkward position in the same manner that the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood would have been- they have a conspiracy with very similar themes in the same book (see Operation Nebula)<br /> <br /> Also, I think that the Core have ended up including that Division 6 are now part of TFV (which, you don't doesn't really make much sense), so that may have been part of the reason. Still, KotS are here, which is a very pleasant surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T11:27:09-07:00","id":1515956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515953#post1515953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Division 6 would have been in a very awkward position in the same manner that the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood would have been- they have a conspiracy with very similar themes in the same book (see Operation Nebula)<br /> <br /> Also, I think that the Core have ended up including that Division 6 are now part of TFV (which, you don't doesn't really make much sense), so that may have been part of the reason. Still, KotS are here, which is a very pleasant surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I respectfully disagree with division 6 and operation nebula, I somewhat agree on the latter. Only somewhat, but I feel it was probably due to the backlash concerning the folding of compacts and conspiracies that they didn't just become a conspiracy. In which I will admit I was part of the party who was vocal about disliking that.<br /> <br /> But the Sisterhood is based more in the occult than the Survivors club it seems. I don't know, It's probably the only time I've ever been thinking &quot;ehh they probably could have just added this to a preexisting group&quot; rather than &quot;oh cool, what can be further done to flesh out this new group?&quot;. Even then, that was only initial. I do think both can coexist without feeling too much of the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-23-2023, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T22:00:26-07:00","id":1515985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515953#post1515953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think that the Core have ended up including that Division 6 are now part of TFV (which, you don't doesn't really make much sense), so that may have been part of the reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corebook says that there's a conspiracy theory that Division Six and the Barrett Commission were dissolved and had their active members reassigned to TFV, which is <i>explicitly</i> a conspiracy theory in the part of the setting overview chapter that specifically is talking about Hunter's particular version of &quot;the Chronicles of Darkness is a setting where even the monsters are getting news about their peers through the lens of furtive rumor and urban legends.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only statement of fact in that paragraph is that TFV is the only government-sanctioned hunter group still officially on the books and that even that may change in the future \u2014 setting aside people's complaints about it happening, observe that VASCU's fate demonstrates how this doesn't actually have to mean the group no longer exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T22:05:56-07:00","id":1515986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515953#post1515953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Division 6 would have been in a very awkward position in the same manner that the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood would have been- they have a conspiracy with very similar themes in the same book (see Operation Nebula)<br /> <br /> Also, I think that the Core have ended up including that Division 6 are now part of TFV (which, you don't doesn't really make much sense), so that may have been part of the reason. Still, KotS are here, which is a very pleasant surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I respectfully disagree with division 6 and operation nebula, I somewhat agree on the latter. Only somewhat, but I feel it was probably due to the backlash concerning the folding of compacts and conspiracies that they didn't just become a conspiracy. In which I will admit I was part of the party who was vocal about disliking that. <br /> But the Sisterhood is based more in the occult than the Survivors club it seems. I don't know, It's probably the only time I've ever been thinking &quot;ehh they probably could have just added this to a preexisting group&quot; rather than &quot;oh cool, what can be further done to flesh out this new group?&quot;. Even then, that was only initial. I do think both can coexist without feeling too much of the same<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T10:23:56-07:00","id":1516109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1515986#post1515986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I respectfully disagree with division 6 and operation nebula, I somewhat agree on the latter. Only somewhat, but I feel it was probably due to the backlash concerning the folding of compacts and conspiracies that they didn't just become a conspiracy. In which I will admit I was part of the party who was vocal about disliking that.<br /> But the Sisterhood is based more in the occult than the Survivors club it seems. I don't know, It's probably the only time I've ever been thinking &quot;ehh they probably could have just added this to a preexisting group&quot; rather than &quot;oh cool, what can be further done to flesh out this new group?&quot;. Even then, that was only initial. I do think both can coexist without feeling too much of the same</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that I don't think that the two organizations have a complete overlap with each other (same for the Survivors and the Sisterhood), but considering that ON runs heavily on the &quot;conspiracy theorists&quot; theme, which Division 6 also express, it could have been a bit &quot;awkward&quot; to have both in the same book. Probably in the same manner that if the Ashwood Abbey and the Hunts Club were introduced in the same book it might have been awkward as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T10:37:15-07:00","id":1516110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1516109#post1516109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that I don't think that the two organizations have a complete overlap with each other (same for the Survivors and the Sisterhood), but considering that ON runs heavily on the &quot;conspiracy theorists&quot; theme, which Division 6 also express, it could have been a bit &quot;awkward&quot; to have both in the same book. Probably in the same manner that if the Ashwood Abbey and the Hunts Club were introduced in the same book it might have been awkward as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I just don't consider it as much due to having both the long night and malleus maleficaraum in the same book<br /> <br /> As an aside, honestly the emergent God machine theory for operation nebula probably has more thematic sense for a conspiracy Utopia Now. Damn I I wish they got that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T14:15:01-07:00","id":1517820,"title":"","content":"So I haven't laid out a similar listicle of my thoughts and feelings on the TtF Conspiracies, but it was long enough since the last time that I decided that, hey, we'll wait until the book was now publicly available.<br /> <br /> So on that note, Tending the Flame is <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/441676/Tending-the-Flame-The-Hunter-The-Vigil-Second-Edition-Companion?src=newest_since\" target=\"_blank\">now available on DriveThruRPG</a> in both PDF and Print options! So to help create motives for buying it, let's talk Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> 8) The White Hare Society: Whenever I think I'm doing the White Hare Society dirty by placing them at the bottom, I remind myself I started the section on them with &quot;otherworldly conquistadors&quot; and ended on &quot;we explore otherworlds&quot;-not &quot;otherworldly explorers&quot;, just &quot;we explore otherworlds. To borrow from a complaint about some of the compacts, the conspiracies whole starts and ends with it's concept, which is weird for something that has an admixture of &quot;otherworldly conquistadors&quot;, &quot;Alice in Wonderland/Mirrorland as organizational basis&quot;, and &quot;going native&quot; raised in it's write up. It's endowment is also another case that starts promising and ends up muddled, starting with adjusting themselves to their otherworlds in a way that also wrecks their minds, and ends on kind of coming down as an Elixir knock-off by way of Bioshock (and I suspect Dark Souls, but I can't pin it). I'm loathe to readily name something as bad, and I wouldn't go so far as to call the White Hare Society as such, but for something that was on the edge of Columbus founds Rapture in Wonderland, it's kind of bland, and that has to be noted.<br /> <br /> 7) Watchers: This should be my jam-I'm down for recurring cycles and reincarnation as major motifs, and I'm always in the corner of Mummy's metaphysics and cosmology, and I am in the camp that wish Fable 3's second half had been better designed, and the Watchers are that in spades. But again, the idea never moves past the concept of accessing past lives, and while arguably it's Endowment is more coherent than the White Hare Society, it also doesn't have a lot of spice to it. Again not bad, and it doesn't promise so much it bugs me like the Hares, but it's kind of just there.<br /> <br /> 6) Asclepeion: LostLight highlighted the dream medics as their take on the most complete idea of a conspiracy, and while I disagree, I completely get where they're coming from. The dream medics are a fascinating concept that's pretty well executed, and really feels like a sustained network. That said, I feel like the idea falls a little short in explanation-the Asclepeion play more like &quot;sleepwalking healer-monks smiting the undead&quot; on the whole, and while the dedication to their role as healers, it is their powerset that where I take the most issue with them-well, that and the design of the conspiracy betrays what I regard as a failing of Hunter 2nd Edition on the whole, but we're not here about that. For the most part, Enkiomesis is a weird combo of being kind of over-powered and narrow at the same time. You might be thinking about the way that it lets the medics hit the undead like a truck, and yeah, these guys wreck shop in graveyards, but honestly, I mean more that the healing itself is really powerful-having one of these guys on the scene can make threats need to step up a bit to keep being threats. But there's also just that everything these guys can do is based around healing? I think some people will hear &quot;dream-medic&quot; and wonder if we're going to see them be a peer to the Merrick Institute, or possibly pull some Beast shenanigans by dragging dreams spaces out into the waking world, but nope, just healing. Still, we're getting really solid here, so good.<br /> <br /> 5) Operation Nebula: The only reason they're on this side of the divide of 8 is because I know I will always basically just slap them on as part of another conspiracy because of an arbitrary decision I made years ago, which means it's a me problem keeping them so low-but this is my list, so. Quite simply, this conspiracy slaps. The decision to settle on &quot;aliens&quot; as a particular enemy is an inspired idea, on the grounds that it's really versatile in what it means-the author interpreted it as all monsters, but I had a ready read of them being demons and changelings, and the fact that you can probably argue up and down that scale, or even to different ends, means that you have a lot of versatility in how to handle them both in the game and out of them, and leads to a lot internal and external dynamics that makes for good storytelling. The choices of factions is absolutely solidly playable as character archetypes, and the entire thing being wrapped up in the paranoia and mechanics of conspiracy theories just tells you everything you need to know about how this groups operates, up to and including a real sense that there's skeletons in the closet regarding the central node of coordination for the Conspiracy. Xenotechnology is also brilliant, not only because this is exactly how you want to get into the power and frustrations of working with alien technology, but because it feeds right back into the feel of the whole conspiracy. The entire thing works so well I would say anyone asking what conspiracy I could possibly throw them in with to be worth it has a valid question, and my answer is only going to piss them off.<br /> <br /> Because it's Task Force Valkyrie. Because I decided they had an alien thing because of Roswell really opening doors for them on the subject.<br /> <br /> Look, I never claimed this was a good idea, just one that I was always going to do.<br /> <br /> 4) The Engimatics: Man, what a bunch of weaselly, up their own ass bunch of artistic hack sell-outs, trying to pretend they don't really bother anyone or anything, just chasing their muse and trying to keep a rein on their masterworks, like they aren't hunters violating the privacy of monster's lives or the sanctity of other people's free will.<br /> <br /> I kind of love them. I'm not entirely sure if it reaches beyond they are a bunch of weaselly, up their own ass bunch of artistic hack sell-outs. Given that I readily believe them to be a Deceived project probably goes a long way in that direction, given the Deceived are probably one of my top favorite antagonists in Chronicles. Inspiration also just slaps, with the base mechanic being extremely flavorful and all the Masterworks being equal parts delightfully messed up and darkly utilitarian. The conspiracy on the whole is great for opening up Hunter's conversation on what harm is and what extent and manner can it be justified with before it goes too far. It just, it speaks to me, as a cursed piece of literature should do.<br /> <br /> 3) Campion Wildlife Services: The more it's argued that this should be a compact, the more I love this Conspiracy-which is weird, because I get and even agree with the complaints. In a lot of ways, this feels really small scale-even the endowment feels mostly like an exaggeration of what the average joe would think most animal control does have to deal with animals, and it's hard to imagine this being of a particular scale. But I dunno, I just really love this conspiracy. Maybe it's because, even if it feels like a compact, it feels like a 1st Edition compact-something in the flavor hits in a way a lot of 2nd Edition doesn't. Maybe it's because they're the closest organization to being the most morally upright, or at least morally uncomplicated, in the entire Hunter canon, and the fact I have to add qualifiers like &quot;most&quot; or &quot;least&quot; does a lot to explain how such a simple idea can become complicated real quick and how the morality that Hunter explores actually works. Maybe it's because I do recognize that, while it's not Advanced Armory levels of crazy, there's absolutely a step up here compared to it's real world counterparts. Mostly, I kind of get a feeling that it's like &quot;the little conspiracy that could&quot;, where the more it seems like it should be a compact, the more you want to root for it as a conspiracy-and I think that blurring of how those words are used it mostly a net positive. Keep it up Campion, and don't let anyone knock you down.<br /> <br /> 2) Aegis Kai Doru:If you're thinking they got this spot because it's riding on the high of all of it's other material, you'd be right. That should lead to your next question, being &quot;why is it not number 1, then?&quot; which I'm happy to explain. Out of the four organizations that got updated to 2nd Edition, AKD is not the one that needed the most updates, by a long shot, but there's a lot of quality of life adjustments that I'm disappointed in not seeing. On the mechanical front, things like the Zeus Stone acting as a magical RFID network for Relics is one of those things C&amp;C came up with that seems like it should just be baked into the conspiracy from here on (even if you don't want to waste your space on the Zeus Stone as an actual Relic), and my supposition that they wanted to hold off on introducing the AKD before giving some serious thought on how to square their conflict with witches has only yielded the one change (which I'm positive about, but we'll get back to that). On the &quot;fluff&quot;, I find it disappointing they weren't able to better incorporate the conspiracy's skeletons into the text, particularly that the Circle and highest heads of AKD want to become wizards again. And also, the selection of Relics was lackluster, not even going over some of the most interesting of older Relic selection and only adding Wonder Woman's lasso as a new item. That said, there is one change that warrant the high ranking in my opinion, and that's by expanding the oath from mages and werewolves to those who work magic and shifters- a much broader focus that is useful on a lot of front and introduces a lot of dynamics, not to mention that it handily accomodates arguments for both the Arisen and Beasts to be regarded as enemies of note to AKD. That, and all the bias for previous material, is what lands it here.<br /> <br /> 1) Survivor's Club: I want to argue that someone enjoyed Scream 6 as much as I did, but that's robbing Peter to market Paul, to murder the saying. That asides, this is just my jam. Smart enough to not just stop at the final girl trope, but to connect towards a general survivorship, I think you could argue that this was the conspiracy people expected with Slasher, but man alive am I glad it let this notion stew a little bit, and has the contrast to VASCU. Maybe it particularly hits because I'm used to people who suffered from horrible action then turning around for whatever reason and saying that that horrible action may be justified looking at other people, but the particulars of survivor's running the risk of buying into Slasher mentality, and even being empowered by briefly connecting to that same darkness is just powerful for me. You honestly can't make a more summary case of what Hunter's about than with the Survivor's Club, trying to overcome trauma while still being shaped by it, and the wrestling match of not letting that darkness define you too much without denying it's reality, and what that should mean about how you deal with more of the same going out there-like, the Survivor's Club is just pitch perfect encapsulation. It's also fucking cool as well as a mechanical tool for characters even before you get to the Horror Within. It's really just my jam, and hopefully good reason for you to grab Tending the Flame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T13:05:05-07:00","id":1518560,"title":"","content":"I like Las Guada\u00f1as in that I like having a criminal compact that aren't about taking out competition from monsters, but actually see their hunting as sacred. I know there are the Ascending Ones too, but the criminal element is only part of them.<br /> <br /> I like having a group that focusses on humanlike monsters, especially since the focus of the second edition has shifted away from that a bit. The Eden Covenant are cock-ends, though.<br /> <br /> Crimson Halo are great.<br /> <br /> I also like the Survivor's Club, though I would have liked the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood to be back too. I mean have both and keep the relationship between them, because having two hunter groups related in that way would be interesting.<br /> <br /> The Enigmatics seem more like a weird cult than a hunter group, but I guess we don't have a Cultist: the Mania line for them to go in.<br /> <br /> Cambion Animal Control sound like they're fighting Deviant conspiracies and humanely putting Manticores down. Which sounds great until you realise they might be putting Deviants down too.<br /> <br /> I like that some the Endowments feel like the same <i>sort</i> of weirdness as Advanced Armoury, Elixirs, or Thaumotech, just different in the details because those researching them had different goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28116-tzies","name":"Tzies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T04:57:21-07:00","id":1538353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1517820#post1517820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Operation Nebula: The only reason they're on this side of the divide of 8 is because I know I will always basically just slap them on as part of another conspiracy because of an arbitrary decision I made years ago, which means it's a me problem keeping them so low-but this is my list, so. Quite simply, this conspiracy slaps. The decision to settle on &quot;aliens&quot; as a particular enemy is an inspired idea, on the grounds that it's really versatile in what it means-the author interpreted it as all monsters, but I had a ready read of them being demons and changelings, and the fact that you can probably argue up and down that scale, or even to different ends, means that you have a lot of versatility in how to handle them both in the game and out of them, and leads to a lot internal and external dynamics that makes for good storytelling. The choices of factions is absolutely solidly playable as character archetypes, and the entire thing being wrapped up in the paranoia and mechanics of conspiracy theories just tells you everything you need to know about how this groups operates, up to and including a real sense that there's skeletons in the closet regarding the central node of coordination for the Conspiracy. Xenotechnology is also brilliant, not only because this is exactly how you want to get into the power and frustrations of working with alien technology, but because it feeds right back into the feel of the whole conspiracy. The entire thing works so well I would say anyone asking what conspiracy I could possibly throw them in with to be worth it has a valid question, and my answer is only going to piss them off.<br /> <br /> Because it's Task Force Valkyrie. Because I decided they had an alien thing because of Roswell really opening doors for them on the subject.<br /> <br /> Look, I never claimed this was a good idea, just one that I was always going to do.<br /> <br /> 4) The Engimatics: Man, what a bunch of weaselly, up their own ass bunch of artistic hack sell-outs, trying to pretend they don't really bother anyone or anything, just chasing their muse and trying to keep a rein on their masterworks, like they aren't hunters violating the privacy of monster's lives or the sanctity of other people's free will.<br /> <br /> I kind of love them. I'm not entirely sure if it reaches beyond they are a bunch of weaselly, up their own ass bunch of artistic hack sell-outs. Given that I readily believe them to be a Deceived project probably goes a long way in that direction, given the Deceived are probably one of my top favorite antagonists in Chronicles. Inspiration also just slaps, with the base mechanic being extremely flavorful and all the Masterworks being equal parts delightfully messed up and darkly utilitarian. The conspiracy on the whole is great for opening up Hunter's conversation on what harm is and what extent and manner can it be justified with before it goes too far. It just, it speaks to me, as a cursed piece of literature should do.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Operation Nebula isn't a branch of TF:V, they're a rival, a garage-tech funhouse mirror of TF:V. And that's okay. Consider soul stones as a source of alien cores; see the Supernal Anchor merit from Summoners, M:tA 1st edition. With no way of actually summoning supernal entities, how do they get them? Why, by hunting Bound supernals in Ruins of the Time Before. This annoys mages because the Nebuloids get their grubby souls all over the Ruins, but mages wouldn't be above manipulating them into kicking over someone else's Demesne...<br /> <br /> The Enigmatics could be associated with the Deceived, but I'd make them their own janky and accidental recreation of the Miasma of Glamour and Azoth from the Seven Wonders setting of Dark Eras 2. And some of them, just some, with no particular pattern, &quot;graduate&quot; into Eternals from M:tC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T21:57:42-07:00","id":1538462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1538353#post1538353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Operation Nebula isn't a branch of TF:V, they're a rival, a garage-tech funhouse mirror of TF:V. And that's okay. Consider soul stones as a source of alien cores; see the Supernal Anchor merit from Summoners, M:tA 1st edition. With no way of actually summoning supernal entities, how do they get them? Why, by hunting Bound supernals in Ruins of the Time Before. This annoys mages because the Nebuloids get their grubby souls all over the Ruins, but mages wouldn't be above manipulating them into kicking over someone else's Demesne...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;I never claimed this was a good idea, just one that I was always going to do.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T12:00:15-07:00","id":1538485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1514790-tending-the-flame-coming-soon?p=1538462#post1538462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See &quot;I never claimed this was a good idea, just one that I was always going to do.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I put that wrong. I just meant that even if you're having TF:V as an alien-focused Conspiracy, that doesn't mean that they work with Nebula.<br /> <br /> People who agree on <i>almost </i>everything can be the deadliest of foes.<br /> <br /> If you know old WoD, think of Nebula as Sons of Ether and TF:V as Void Engineers. Only cash-strapped and mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}